# Social login setup checklist (backend)

> Generated by `php artisan auth:setup` (the light-it auth package). It lists what the
> package could not do for you, because it never edits your files. Tick each box,
> then **delete this file**. How social login works:
> https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/social-login.md

- [ ] **Run `php artisan migrate`** (creates the `social_accounts` table).
- [ ] **Create a Google OAuth client** in the Google Cloud console (APIs & Services →
  Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application). Add every frontend
  URL to **Authorized JavaScript origins** (`http://localhost:5173` for local development).
  No redirect URI is needed.
- [ ] **Set the client id** in `.env` (read by `config/social-login.php`). Google sign-in fails
  until it is set; the frontend uses the same value as `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`:

```dotenv
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
```

Check it worked: `php artisan route:list --path=auth/social` lists
`POST api/auth/social/{provider}`, and `php artisan config:show social-login.google.client_id`
shows your client id.

Adding Apple, Facebook or another provider later is a new `SocialProvider` class plus one
line in `config/social-login.php`; see "Adding a provider" in the doc linked above.
